   "intro": "<p>The open web, reached through Tavily. It carries what a search turns up (hits, the cleaned text of a page, a site's link graph), a synthesised answer pulled from many searches, and looked-up facts about a company or person. This is a builtin tool, always on, never connected, so there is no data gap here. It forms no opinion: a <code>Research report</code> answer is Tavily's synthesis, not the tool's read, and <code>Enrichment</code> facts come from the open web and are only as good as what is published there.</p>\n<p>Owned by Connections, fetched fresh each time and carried untouched. Each record below is a lineage anchor. Its id is the kebab-slug of its label (<code>Web result</code> becomes <code>web-result</code>), and that is what the modules' assemblies reference.</p>",
